//? Title: Cross-Validation: Selection Without Fold Leakage
//? Subtitle: Weight fold losses by validation size and refit after selecting
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A model setting must be selected without letting validation observations fit its preprocessing
or parameters. We inspect unequal folds and use a callback that refits a linear model on each
training partition. Sample-weighted scores distinguish mean error per observation from mean
error per fold; a separate final test remains outside selection.
)
\toc

> The method

KFold creates k validation partitions with sizes floor(N/k) or ceil(N/k), each row held out
exactly once. Each training set is the complement. StratifiedKFold distributes each class after
seeded shuffling and requires at least k examples per class. A callback receives only the two
index lists; it is responsible for fitting preprocessing and model from the training list.

$$
\widehat R=\frac{\sum_f n_f\overline L_f}{\sum_f n_f}.
$$
\alttext(Cross-validation averages fold mean losses weighted by the number of held-out observations in each fold.)

This equals the mean of all out-of-fold observation losses. An unweighted average gives equal
influence to unequal folds. Select settings by this development score, refit on all development
rows, and evaluate a separate test set once. The selected CV score has selection optimism.
Random folds are inappropriate for temporal dependence or grouped observations that must remain
together. The split helper validates coverage but does not enforce callback leakage discipline.

The concept diagram has a retained TikZ source in `diagrams/cross_validation_concept.tikz`.
Regeneration requires LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, and dvisvgm.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/cross_validation_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/cross_validation_concept.tikz > build/cross_validation_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/cross_validation_concept.svg build/cross_validation_concept.dvi > build/cross_validation_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered build/cross_validation_concept.svg from local TikZ source.\n'
```
