> Simple examples

Seven rows split into three unshuffled folds have validation sizes 3,2,2. Artificial fold means 1,2,3 give weighted error 13/7 rather than the unweighted value 2.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cross_validation_sizes.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

int main() {
  namespace m = dm::nn::ml;
  const auto folds = m::KFold(7, 3, 7, false);
  size_t f = 0;
  const auto score = m::CrossValidate(folds, [&](const auto &, const auto &) {
    return double(++f);
  });
  std::vector<double> index, size;
  for (size_t i = 0; i < folds.size(); ++i) {
    index.push_back(i);
    size.push_back(folds[i].validation.size());
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.bars(index, size, "validation rows", {37, 99, 235}, .5)
      .title("Remainder rows make fold sizes unequal")
      .x_label("fold index")
      .y_label("rows")
      .y_limits(0, 4);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  p.size(820, 420).save_svg("build/cross_validation_sizes.svg");
  if (std::abs(score.mean - 13. / 7) > 1e-12)
    return 1;
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame t;
  t.add_column("fold", index);
  t.add_column("validation_rows", size);
  t.add_column("mean_loss", score.fold_losses);
  std::print("{}\n\nSample-weighted mean: {:.9f}; unweighted mean: 2.\n", t.to_md(),
             score.mean);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| fold | validation_rows | mean_loss |
| ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 0 | 3 | 1 |
| 1 | 2 | 2 |
| 2 | 2 | 3 |


Sample-weighted mean: 1.857142857; unweighted mean: 2.
\image(figures/cross_validation_sizes.svg)
// result_end
